From 2b81db46ba2fb498b4d6ba51e7590d0fd5291f0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 15:10:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0106 -- SB 8-bit-DMA unblock (PicoGUS-in-SB-mode)
 + DMA-path diag

g2k can run a PicoGUS card in Sound Blaster mode, but it is an 8-bit-DMA,
SB2.0-class device with no high (16-bit) DMA channel. It still reports DSP
4.x, so the pre-patch detection predicate (soundblaster_is_sb16 =
!FORCE_SB_8BIT && version>=4) latched is_sb16=true and OpenDevice committed
to a 16-bit transfer on the BLASTER H channel that the card cannot perform:
it hard-errored ("No high (16-bit) DMA channel") when BLASTER had no H, or
armed a 16-bit DMA whose IRQ-5 never fired. Because the Organya / OPL3 /
WaveBlaster pumps all ride the SB DMA-IRQ callback, every backend died
silent together (while Doom, which drives 8-bit D-channel DMA directly,
worked on the same card).

Why DOS needs this: there is no 16-bit DMA path on an 8-bit SB-class card,
so "DSP version >= 4" is the wrong proxy for "use the 16-bit high-DMA path."
This patch decouples them at the single detection site:

  1. FORCE_SB_8BIT promoted to a runtime hint
     SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_FORCE_8BIT (strict-"1", default 0=OFF);
     the compile-time #define is retained as an OR'd override.
  2. is_sb16 now also requires soundblaster_highdma_channel >= 0 (a real H
     token in BLASTER). A DSP-4.x card with no H GRACEFULLY falls back to
     the existing 8-bit low-DMA D-channel path instead of OpenDevice's hard
     SDL_SetError. The entire pre-SB16 path (format/channel, DMA pick, 8-bit
     controller program, 0x40/0x48/0x1C DSP start, isr_is_16bit) is already
     coherently keyed off this one flag, so the flip routes the whole open
     down the working 8-bit path with no per-site edits.

BYTE-IDENTICAL for the shipped Vibra16 + H5 case: real SB16 reports
version>=4 AND BLASTER carries H5 (highdma=5>=0) AND the hint defaults OFF,
so is_sb16 stays exactly !FORCE_SB_8BIT && (version>=4) == true -- the
identical value the pre-patch predicate produced; every downstream is_sb16
consumer takes the same branch. DOSBox-X (sbtype=sb16, emulates H5) holds
is_sb16=true too. The new term only changes the result for a DSP-4.x card
that lacks an H channel, or when the hint/override forces 8-bit.

Diagnostics (all via doskutsu_dbg_log -> <TAG>SDL.LOG; positioned to answer
"where does it die"):
  - unconditional DMA-path decision banner at detection (is_sb16/force_8bit/
    dsp_ver/highdma -> path), plus a loud graceful-fallback witness;
  - OpenDevice DMA-programmed line (path, DMA channel + register family,
    format, channels, rate, IRQ, ack port, silence value);
  - DSP start-command-sequence witness in each of the 16-bit and 8-bit
    branches;
  - OpenDevice SUCCESS witness (path + IRQ count at open);
  - CloseDevice run-end witness: total IRQ-5 fires (0 == DMA-IRQ never armed
    -> silence is upstream of the ISR), reusing doskutsu_audio_irq_count;
  - CloseDevice WB/MPU witness: doskutsu_mpu_write_count + the bit-6 DRR
    poll-timeout count doskutsu_mpu_drr_cap_hits, to confirm/deny the
    wave-40 REFUTE_MPU_TIMEOUT (DreamBlaster S2 output-busy-after-byte-1)
    signature recurs on this card.

Completion (SDL/0106, sdl-engine): adopted the above as the slot base and
finished the contract: (a) synth.c WaveBlaster init-RESULT witness at the
end of SDL_DOSMpu401Init (OK/FAILED + resolved DRR-poll state + drr_cap +
running drr_cap_hits), the init-time companion of the sb.c CloseDevice
WB/MPU run-end witness -- together they bracket the wave-40 REFUTE_MPU_TIMEOUT
field; (b) refreshed the stale compile-time-only FORCE_SB_8BIT comment to
document the runtime hint. Vibra16+H5 byte-identical property re-verified
independently: hint-off + DSP>=4 + highdma>=0 yields the identical is_sb16
value and the identical downstream branch; added code on that path is
log-only (no register writes, no control-flow change).

Workspace-local patch; not upstreamed (sdl_ai_policy).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c    | 172 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c |  28 ++++-
 2 files changed, 194 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 578f7bf8a..842d14040 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -47,8 +47,15 @@ extern volatile bool g_dos_audio_pause_request;
 extern volatile bool g_dos_audio_resume_request;
 extern SDL_DOSIdlePauseCallback g_dos_audio_idle_pause_cb;
 
-// Set to 1 to force 8-bit mono (pre-SB16) code path even on SB16 hardware.
-// Useful for testing in DOSBox which always emulates an SB16 (DSP 4.x).
+// DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0106): forcing the pre-SB16 8-bit / D-channel path is
+// now primarily a RUNTIME knob -- SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_FORCE_8BIT (strict
+// "1", default OFF), resolved in IsSoundBlasterPresent() and OR'd with this
+// #define. The PicoGUS-in-SB-mode / SB2.0-class case (DSP 4.x but no 16-bit
+// high DMA) also reaches the 8-bit path automatically via the highdma>=0 term
+// there (graceful fallback), so this hint is mainly for forcing 8-bit on a card
+// that DOES advertise high DMA. This compile-time #define is retained as an
+// additional source-level override: set it to 1 to force 8-bit unconditionally
+// (e.g. a bisecting build), which still wins regardless of the runtime hint.
 #define FORCE_SB_8BIT 0
 
 static int soundblaster_base_port = -1;
@@ -65,7 +72,7 @@ static int soundblaster_dma_channel = -1;
 static int soundblaster_highdma_channel = -1;
 static int soundblaster_version = -1;
 static int soundblaster_version_minor = -1;
-static bool soundblaster_is_sb16 = false; // false when FORCE_SB_8BIT or DSP < 4
+static bool soundblaster_is_sb16 = false; // SDL/0106: false when force-8bit (hint/#define), DSP < 4, or no high (16-bit) DMA channel
 static Uint8 soundblaster_silence_value = 0;
 
 /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0050): killswitch state for the
@@ -2617,6 +2624,24 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
     // Cache the IRQ ack port so the ISR doesn't chase pointers.
     isr_irq_ack_port = is_sb16 ? (soundblaster_base_port + 0x0F) : (soundblaster_base_port + 0x0E);
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0106): OpenDevice DMA-path diagnostic. Records the
+       path actually committed (chosen path, programmed DMA channel + page/
+       offset/count register family, resolved sample format + channels + rate,
+       IRQ + ack-port), so the PicoGUS-SB iter log shows exactly what the DMA
+       controller was programmed with. The DSP command sequence is logged
+       separately in each start branch below (SDL/0106). Always-on (read-only
+       snapshot at open; no killswitch). */
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0106 OpenDevice DMA programmed: path=%s "
+                     "dma_ch=%d (%s) dma_buflen=%d fmt=0x%X ch=%d freq=%d Hz "
+                     "irq=%d ack_port=0x%X silence=0x%02X",
+                     is_sb16 ? "16-bit-high-DMA" : "8-bit-low-DMA",
+                     hidden->dma_channel,
+                     is_sb16 ? "high/word ports 0xC0-0xDF" : "low/byte ports 0x00-0x0F",
+                     (int)hidden->dma_buflen,
+                     (unsigned)device->spec.format, device->spec.channels,
+                     device->spec.freq, soundblaster_irq,
+                     (unsigned)isr_irq_ack_port, soundblaster_silence_value);
+
     // Set up the IRQ-driven ring buffer.
     hidden->chunk_size = device->buffer_size; // one DMA half-buffer
 
@@ -2791,6 +2816,13 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
         WriteSoundBlasterDSP((Uint8)(block_size & 0xFF));
         WriteSoundBlasterDSP((Uint8)(block_size >> 8));
 
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0106): DSP start-command-sequence witness for
+           the 16-bit (is_sb16) path. */
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0106 DSP start seq (16-bit): 0xD1(spkr-on) "
+                         "0x41 rate=%d 0xB6(autoinit/FIFO) 0x30(S16-stereo) "
+                         "block_size=%d (words-1)",
+                         device->spec.freq, block_size);
+
         /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0074 Part 2): SB16 CT1745 analog
            mixer balance lever. The SB16 driver historically programs only
            the DSP rate + DMA (and the SB Pro 0x0E stereo bit on the pre-
@@ -2908,6 +2940,18 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
         // rare and would need single-cycle transfers re-triggered from the ISR.
         // For now we use 0x1C anyway and hope for the best on DSP 1.x hardware.
         WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0x1C); // 8-bit auto-init DMA playback
+
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0106): DSP start-command-sequence witness for
+           the 8-bit (pre-SB16 / PicoGUS-SB / SB2.0-class) path. This is the
+           sequence the PicoGUS-SB now reaches after the SDL/0106 graceful
+           fall-back; if IRQ-5 still never fires, the OpenDevice-DMA + this
+           line bracket exactly where the chip was last touched. */
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0106 DSP start seq (8-bit): 0xD1(spkr-on) "
+                         "0x40 tc=%d (rate=%d effective=%d) 0x48 block_size=%d "
+                         "(bytes-1) 0x1C(8-bit autoinit)%s",
+                         (int)time_constant, device->spec.freq, effective_rate,
+                         block_size,
+                         (soundblaster_version >= 3) ? " +mixer0x0E stereo-bit" : "");
     }
 
     SDL_Log("SoundBlaster opened!");
@@ -2947,6 +2991,18 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
        at CloseDevice. The single OpenDevice success exit; the early failure return
        is before any IRQ/DMA arm so the flag correctly stays false there. */
     g_dos_sb_device_open = true;
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0106): single OpenDevice success witness. Pairs
+       with the per-early-return SDL_SetError strings (which the engine's
+       audio-init narration already surfaces on failure) so the iter log has
+       an unambiguous "the SB device opened on the %s path" marker. Snapshots
+       the IRQ-fire count at open (should be 0 here, before any IRQ has fired)
+       so the CloseDevice delta = IRQ-5 fires during the run. */
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0106 OpenDevice SUCCESS path=%s dma_ch=%d "
+                     "irq=%d irq_count_at_open=%lu",
+                     is_sb16 ? "16-bit-high-DMA" : "8-bit-low-DMA",
+                     hidden->dma_channel, soundblaster_irq,
+                     (unsigned long)doskutsu_audio_irq_count);
     return true;
 }
 
@@ -3813,6 +3869,32 @@ static void DOSSOUNDBLASTER_CloseDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
        cold-init after this close sees a cold bus again. Unconditional (safe even
        if hidden is NULL -- then nothing was hot anyway). */
     g_dos_sb_device_open = false;
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0106): IRQ-5-fire counter at CloseDevice. The
+       decisive "did the SB DMA IRQ ever fire" witness -- doskutsu_audio_irq_count
+       increments once per IRQ-5 in SoundBlasterIRQHandler. For a card whose
+       DMA-IRQ never armed (the pre-patch PicoGUS-SB failure shape) this reads
+       0 here, telling the analyst the silence is upstream of the ISR (the DMA
+       never started) rather than in the mix path. Logged before any teardown
+       so it reflects the whole run. */
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0106 CloseDevice: total IRQ-5 fires this run = "
+                     "%lu (0 == DMA-IRQ never armed; the pumps never ran)",
+                     (unsigned long)doskutsu_audio_irq_count);
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0106): WaveBlaster-path run-end witness. The MPU-401
+       init RESULT is logged at init time in SDL_dos_audio_synth.c (the
+       'mpu401: ... init at port_base=...' lines); here we surface the run-end
+       totals so a single CloseDevice block answers whether the wave-40
+       REFUTE_MPU_TIMEOUT signature recurs on this card: doskutsu_mpu_drr_cap_hits
+       is the bit-6 DRR (Data-Ready-to-Receive) poll-timeout count (the g2k
+       DreamBlaster S2 "output-buffer-busy stuck after byte 1" stall), and
+       doskutsu_mpu_write_count is the total MPU bytes pushed. drr_cap_hits>0
+       with write_count stalling near 1 == the MPU-output-busy wedge reproduced;
+       drr_cap_hits==0 with write_count climbing == MPU output is healthy. */
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0106 CloseDevice WB/MPU witness: "
+                     "mpu_write_count=%lu drr_poll_cap_hits=%lu",
+                     (unsigned long)doskutsu_mpu_write_count,
+                     (unsigned long)doskutsu_mpu_drr_cap_hits);
     if (hidden) {
         /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0043): force-DSP-pause hard-
            reset teardown path. Supersedes the patch 0040 amend's
@@ -4153,8 +4235,88 @@ static bool IsSoundBlasterPresent(void)
     SDL_Log("SB: dma16=%d", soundblaster_highdma_channel);
     SDL_Log("SB: version=%d.%d", soundblaster_version, soundblaster_version_minor);
 
-    soundblaster_is_sb16 = !FORCE_SB_8BIT && (soundblaster_version >= 4);
-    soundblaster_silence_value = soundblaster_is_sb16 ? 0x00 : 0x80; // S16LE silence is 0x00, U8 silence is 0x80
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0106): promote the compile-time FORCE_SB_8BIT
+       knob to a RUNTIME hint, and DECOUPLE "use the 16-bit high-DMA path"
+       from "DSP version >= 4".
+
+       Motivation (PicoGUS-card-in-SB-mode on g2k): a PicoGUS reports DSP
+       4.x (so the pre-patch predicate (version >= 4) latched is_sb16=true)
+       but is an 8-bit-DMA, SB2.0-class device -- it has NO high (16-bit)
+       DMA channel. The whole is_sb16 machinery in OpenDevice (format =
+       S16/stereo, dma_channel = soundblaster_highdma_channel, the 0xB6/0x30
+       16-bit autoinit DSP sequence, the 0xC0-0xDF high-DMA controller
+       programming, isr_is_16bit) then commits to a 16-bit transfer the card
+       cannot perform: OpenDevice either hard-errors at the "No high (16-bit)
+       DMA channel" SDL_SetError below (when BLASTER has no H token) or arms
+       a 16-bit DMA whose IRQ-5 never fires -- and since the Organya / OPL3 /
+       WaveBlaster pumps all ride that DMA-IRQ callback, every backend dies
+       silent together. Doom works on the same card because it drives 8-bit
+       DMA via the D channel + the WaveBlaster header directly.
+
+       Two independent levers:
+         1. force_8bit  -- SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_FORCE_8BIT, strict-"1",
+            default 0 (OFF). =1 forces the pre-SB16 8-bit/D-channel path
+            regardless of DSP version (the old compile-time FORCE_SB_8BIT,
+            now runtime). FORCE_SB_8BIT (the #define) is retained as an OR'd
+            compile-time override so an explicit source flip still wins.
+         2. high-DMA availability -- is_sb16 now additionally requires a
+            high (16-bit) DMA channel to actually be present
+            (soundblaster_highdma_channel >= 0, i.e. BLASTER had an H token).
+            A DSP-4.x card with NO H GRACEFULLY falls back to the 8-bit
+            low-DMA D-channel path instead of the hard SDL_SetError in
+            OpenDevice. This is the structural unblock: the entire pre-SB16
+            path (format/channel select at ~2343, DMA pick at ~2566, the
+            8-bit controller program at ~2601, the 0x40/0x48/0x1C DSP start
+            at ~2879, isr_is_16bit) is already coherently keyed off this one
+            flag, so flipping it here routes the whole open down the working
+            8-bit path with no per-site edits.
+
+       BYTE-IDENTICAL for the shipped Vibra16 + H5 case: a real SB16 reports
+       version >= 4 AND BLASTER carries H5 (highdma_channel = 5 >= 0), and the
+       hint defaults OFF, so is_sb16 stays exactly !FORCE_SB_8BIT && (version
+       >= 4) == true -- the identical value the pre-patch predicate produced.
+       DOSBox-X (sbtype=sb16, emulates H5) likewise holds is_sb16=true. The
+       new term only changes the result for a DSP-4.x card that lacks an H
+       channel or when the hint/override forces 8-bit -- neither of which is
+       the Vibra16 default path. */
+    {
+        const char *f8_hint = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_FORCE_8BIT");
+        const bool force_8bit =
+            FORCE_SB_8BIT ||
+            (f8_hint && f8_hint[0] == '1' && f8_hint[1] == '\0');
+        const bool have_highdma = (soundblaster_highdma_channel >= 0);
+
+        soundblaster_is_sb16 = !force_8bit && (soundblaster_version >= 4) && have_highdma;
+        soundblaster_silence_value = soundblaster_is_sb16 ? 0x00 : 0x80; // S16LE silence is 0x00, U8 silence is 0x80
+
+        /* Unconditional decision banner (mirrors SDL/0073 always-on pattern):
+           routed via doskutsu_dbg_log to <TAG>SDL.LOG so the iter log shows
+           which DMA path this card resolved -- the decisive "where does it
+           die" witness for the PicoGUS-SB case. Required smoke banner. */
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0106 SB DMA-path decision: is_sb16=%d "
+                         "force_8bit=%d dsp_ver=%d highdma=%d -> %s path",
+                         soundblaster_is_sb16 ? 1 : 0,
+                         force_8bit ? 1 : 0,
+                         soundblaster_version,
+                         soundblaster_highdma_channel,
+                         soundblaster_is_sb16 ? "16-bit-high-DMA" : "8-bit-low-DMA");
+
+        /* Loud witness for the specific PicoGUS-SB shape: DSP claims SB16 but
+           there is no high-DMA channel, so we deliberately downshift to the
+           8-bit D-channel path that the pre-patch code would have hard-errored
+           on. Names the force-8bit hint for the operator. */
+        if ((soundblaster_version >= 4) && !have_highdma && !force_8bit) {
+            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0106 DSP %d.%d reports SB16 but BLASTER "
+                             "has no H (high/16-bit DMA) channel -- GRACEFUL "
+                             "fall back to the 8-bit low-DMA D-channel path "
+                             "(D=%d) instead of erroring; this is the "
+                             "PicoGUS-in-SB-mode / SB2.0-class unblock. Set "
+                             "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_FORCE_8BIT=1 to force "
+                             "this path on any card.",
+                             soundblaster_version, soundblaster_version_minor,
+                             soundblaster_dma_channel);
+        }
+    }
 
     return true;
 }
diff --git a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
index e3431f9f3..9dc29b6c3 100644
--- a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
+++ b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
@@ -82,6 +82,11 @@ static bool s_mpu401_use_dsp = false;
    helper added by patch 0080. */
 static bool SDL_DOSMpu401Init_DirectPort(uint16_t port_base);
 static bool SDL_DOSMpu401WaitDRR(uint16_t port_base);
+/* SDL/0106: tentative declaration so the SDL_DOSMpu401Init init-result witness
+   (below, before the canonical definition) can report the resolved DRR-poll
+   state. The full rationale + initialized definition (= false) live with the
+   SDL/0093 DRR-poll opt-in block further down. */
+static bool s_mpu401_drr_poll_enabled;
 
 bool SDL_DOSMpu401Init(uint16_t port_base)
 {
@@ -142,7 +147,28 @@ bool SDL_DOSMpu401Init(uint16_t port_base)
 
     /* === Default path: direct-port MPU-401 + bit-6 DRR polling (patch 0080) === */
     s_mpu401_use_dsp = false;
-    return SDL_DOSMpu401Init_DirectPort(port_base);
+    const bool dp_ok = SDL_DOSMpu401Init_DirectPort(port_base);
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0106): WaveBlaster MPU-401 init-RESULT witness.
+       The companion of the sb.c CloseDevice WB/MPU run-end witness -- this
+       logs, at init time, whether the direct-port bring-up succeeded and the
+       resolved bit-6 DRR-poll configuration. drr_cap_hits is the running
+       poll-timeout counter (the wave-40 REFUTE_MPU_TIMEOUT field: the g2k
+       DreamBlaster S2 "output-buffer-busy stuck after byte 1" signature shows
+       as cap_hits climbing while writes stall); it is normally 0 here at init
+       and accumulates over the run. drr_poll_enabled=0 (the SDL/0093 default)
+       means the status port is never READ, so a poll-timeout cannot occur and
+       cap_hits stays 0 by construction -- in that mode the relevant signal is
+       sb.c's mpu_write_count climbing (bytes accepted) with audible output. */
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("mpu401: SDL/0106 WB init result=%s port_base=0x%04x "
+                     "drr_poll_enabled=%d drr_cap=%u drr_cap_hits=%lu "
+                     "(cap_hits>0 + write stall == wave-40 MPU-busy wedge recurs)",
+                     dp_ok ? "OK" : "FAILED",
+                     (unsigned)port_base,
+                     s_mpu401_drr_poll_enabled ? 1 : 0,
+                     (unsigned)doskutsu_mpu_drr_cap,
+                     (unsigned long)doskutsu_mpu_drr_cap_hits);
+    return dp_ok;
 }
 
 /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0080): bounded bit-6 DRR poll helper.
-- 
2.47.3

